{"seq":2,"time":1789143352346,"type":"request/header","data":{"reason":"initial","system":"Follow the scripted task exactly.\n\n# Tool instructions\n\n## read\n\nUse read on a directory to inspect its sorted immediate entries. Read a file before editing it, then pass its version to edit as expected_version. Continue from the offset in a truncation notice rather than rereading from the start.\n\n## edit\n\nUse edit for every file change. Read an existing file first and include enough surrounding lines in old_text to make each match unique. To create a file, send one edit with empty old_text and the complete file in new_text. Pass the version returned by read as expected_version when the file must be unchanged.\n\n## bash\n\nUse bash to build, test, and run programs. Prefer read, grep, and edit for inspecting and changing files.","tools":[{"name":"read","description":"Read a text file with line numbers or list a directory's immediate entries. Shows at most 2000 lines or 50 KiB per call; when more remains, the result names the offset to continue from. File reads return a sha256 version of the complete bytes. Binary files are reported with their size rather than shown.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Maximum lines or entries to show. Default and cap 2000.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"offset":{"description":"First line or directory entry to show, 1-indexed. Default 1.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"File or directory path, absolute or relative to the first read root.","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"edit","description":"Replace exact text in one file, or create a file with one edit whose old_text is empty. Each nonempty old_text must occur exactly once in the current file; matches must not overlap; all edits are applied together in one atomic write. There is no fuzzy matching: copy old_text exactly, including indentation. Returns a unified diff.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"edits":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"new_text":{"description":"Replacement text.","type":"string"},"old_text":{"description":"Text to find; must occur exactly once. Use an empty string only to create a missing or empty file with one edit.","type":"string"}},"required":["old_text","new_text"],"type":"object"},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"expected_version":{"description":"Optional sha256 version returned by read; the edit is refused when the current bytes differ.","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"File path, absolute or relative to the first read root.","type":"string"}},"required":["path","edits"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"bash","description":"Run a command with /bin/bash -c in the first read root. Times out after timeout_seconds (default 120). Returns stdout, stderr, the exit code, and the duration; a non-zero exit is an ordinary result. The rendering opens with the exit status. At most the last 2000 lines or 50 KiB of output are collected; the rest is saved to a file named in the result.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"command":{"description":"Shell command line.","type":"string"},"timeout_seconds":{"description":"Wall-clock limit. Default 120.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["command"],"type":"object"}}],"model":{"provider":"host","model":"host"}}}
